  "note": "Complete original castle exterior: full irregular outer/double curtain walls, open upper/lower baileys and stepped stone terraces, distinct French/Italian/English/German/round towers and bastions, chapel with minaret, low bath roof, internal museum/range roofs, entry bridges/gates/steps and physically open passages. Town/marina/boats/water, trees/planting, temporary archaeological display objects, museum fit-out and underground chambers are excluded. Retained map supplies plan dimensions and internal footprints but no reliable wall/tower heights. The ordinary official museum visitor page describes the French Tower as47.50m above sea level; use that as a total envelope with explicit original photo-proportional reconstruction. Do not turn it into a47.5m building height above the local hill. Other vertical levels and current gateway/terrace/site grades remain approximate, not surveyed. Original local tower crests:French38.5m(47.5m above sea),Italian32.3m/34.5m roof house,English30.5m,German26.2m,round21m,D-shaped22.3m. Chapel7.5m floor/14.8m eaves/18.5m ridge;minaret33.5m tip. All except French total are original picture proportions, not surveyed. +X ESE toward the east bay,-X WNW toward the marina;+Z SSW toward the seaward/south peninsula tip,-Z NNE toward the town/landward approach;+Y up. The mapped chapel is at local[-29.010,56.713]; the principal east/west tower pair is near[39,30]/[14,34]. Fine named tower association remains original picture/map interpretation."
